{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "multiplication table of the complex numbers (row times column):\n      |   1   i\n  ----+--------\n    1 |   1   i\n    i |   i  -1\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "multiplication_table", "ucas": "table complex", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "multiplication_table", "headline": "multiplication table of the complex numbers (row times column):", "details": ["|   1   i", "----+--------", "1 |   1   i", "i |   i  -1"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "multiplication table of the complex numbers (row times column):\n      |   1   i\n  ----+--------\n    1 |   1   i\n    i |   i  -1\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "multiplication table of the quaternions (row times column), not symmetric: the product does not commute:\n      |   1   i   j   k\n  ----+----------------\n    1 |   1   i   j   k\n    i |   i  -1   k  -j\n    j |   j  -k  -1   i\n    k |   k   j  -i  -1\n  i^2 = j^2 = k^2 = ijk = -1 (Hamilton); ij = k, jk = i, ki = j, and reversing a product changes its sign\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "multiplication_table", "ucas": "table quaternion", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "multiplication_table", "headline": "multiplication table of the quaternions (row times column), not symmetric: the product does not commute:", "details": ["|   1   i   j   k", "----+----------------", "1 |   1   i   j   k", "i |   i  -1   k  -j", "j |   j  -k  -1   i", "k |   k   j  -i  -1", "i^2 = j^2 = k^2 = ijk = -1 (Hamilton); ij = k, jk = i, ki = j, and reversing a product changes its sign"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "multiplication table of the quaternions (row times column), not symmetric: the product does not commute:\n      |   1   i   j   k\n  ----+----------------\n    1 |   1   i   j   k\n    i |   i  -1   k  -j\n    j |   j  -k  -1   i\n    k |   k   j  -i  -1\n  i^2 = j^2 = k^2 = ijk = -1 (Hamilton); ij = k, jk = i, ki = j, and reversing a product changes its sign\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "multiplication table of the octonions (row times column), not symmetric: the product does not commute:\n       |    1   e1   e2   e3   e4   e5   e6   e7\n  -----+----------------------------------------\n     1 |    1   e1   e2   e3   e4   e5   e6   e7\n    e1 |   e1   -1   e3  -e2   e5  -e4  -e7   e6\n    e2 |   e2  -e3   -1   e1   e6   e7  -e4  -e5\n    e3 |   e3   e2  -e1   -1   e7  -e6   e5  -e4\n    e4 |   e4  -e5  -e6  -e7   -1   e1   e2   e3\n    e5 |   e5   e4  -e7   e6  -e1   -1  -e3   e2\n    e6 |   e6   e7   e4  -e5  -e2   e3   -1  -e1\n    e7 |   e7  -e6   e5   e4  -e3  -e2   e1   -1\n  the Fano plane: the 7 lines (a, b, c) with e_a e_b = e_c, e_b e_c = e_a, e_c e_a = e_b:\n    (1, 2, 3) (1, 4, 5) (1, 7, 6) (2, 4, 6) (2, 5, 7) (3, 4, 7) (3, 6, 5)\n  every pair of units lies on one line; e_a^2 = -1 and e_a e_b = -e_b e_a for a != b\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "multiplication_table", "ucas": "table octonion", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "multiplication_table", "the_fano_plane": "the 7 lines (a, b, c) with e_a e_b = e_c, e_b e_c = e_a, e_c e_a = e_b:", "headline": "multiplication table of the octonions (row times column), not symmetric: the product does not commute:", "details": ["|    1   e1   e2   e3   e4   e5   e6   e7", "-----+----------------------------------------", "1 |    1   e1   e2   e3   e4   e5   e6   e7", "e1 |   e1   -1   e3  -e2   e5  -e4  -e7   e6", "e2 |   e2  -e3   -1   e1   e6   e7  -e4  -e5", "e3 |   e3   e2  -e1   -1   e7  -e6   e5  -e4", "e4 |   e4  -e5  -e6  -e7   -1   e1   e2   e3", "e5 |   e5   e4  -e7   e6  -e1   -1  -e3   e2", "e6 |   e6   e7   e4  -e5  -e2   e3   -1  -e1", "e7 |   e7  -e6   e5   e4  -e3  -e2   e1   -1", "(1, 2, 3) (1, 4, 5) (1, 7, 6) (2, 4, 6) (2, 5, 7) (3, 4, 7) (3, 6, 5)", "every pair of units lies on one line; e_a^2 = -1 and e_a e_b = -e_b e_a for a != b"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "multiplication table of the octonions (row times column), not symmetric: the product does not commute:\n       |    1   e1   e2   e3   e4   e5   e6   e7\n  -----+----------------------------------------\n     1 |    1   e1   e2   e3   e4   e5   e6   e7\n    e1 |   e1   -1   e3  -e2   e5  -e4  -e7   e6\n    e2 |   e2  -e3   -1   e1   e6   e7  -e4  -e5\n    e3 |   e3   e2  -e1   -1   e7  -e6   e5  -e4\n    e4 |   e4  -e5  -e6  -e7   -1   e1   e2   e3\n    e5 |   e5   e4  -e7   e6  -e1   -1  -e3   e2\n    e6 |   e6   e7   e4  -e5  -e2   e3   -1  -e1\n    e7 |   e7  -e6   e5   e4  -e3  -e2   e1   -1\n  the Fano plane: the 7 lines (a, b, c) with e_a e_b = e_c, e_b e_c = e_a, e_c e_a = e_b:\n    (1, 2, 3) (1, 4, 5) (1, 7, 6) (2, 4, 6) (2, 5, 7) (3, 4, 7) (3, 6, 5)\n  every pair of units lies on one line; e_a^2 = -1 and e_a e_b = -e_b e_a for a != b\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "the quaternions: dimension 4 over the reals, basis 1, i, j, k\n  commutative: no: i j = k but j i = -k\n  associative: yes ((ab)c = a(bc) at 200 random triples); by Frobenius, R, C and H are the only associative real division algebras\n  alternative: yes ((aa)b = a(ab), (ba)a = b(aa) at 200 random pairs)\n  flexible and power-associative: yes ((ab)a = a(ba); powers a^n are well defined), as in every Cayley-Dickson algebra\n  normed (a composition algebra): yes, |ab| = |a||b| at 200 random pairs (Euler's four-square identity)\n  a division algebra: yes, ab = 0 only when a = 0 or b = 0 (it is normed); by Hurwitz, R, C, H and O are the only normed division algebras\n  inverses: every a != 0 has a^-1 = conj(a)/|a|^2 (a a^-1 = 1, checked)\n  conjugation: conj(ab) = conj(b) conj(a) (checked); a conj(a) = |a|^2\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "algebra", "ucas": "algebra quaternion", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "algebra", "commutative": "no: i j = k but j i = -k", "associative": "yes ((ab)c = a(bc) at 200 random triples); by Frobenius, R, C and H are the only associative real division algebras", "alternative": "yes ((aa)b = a(ab), (ba)a = b(aa) at 200 random pairs)", "flexible_and_power_associative": "yes ((ab)a = a(ba); powers a^n are well defined), as in every Cayley-Dickson algebra", "normed_a_composition_algebra": "yes, |ab| = |a||b| at 200 random pairs (Euler's four-square identity)", "a_division_algebra": "yes, ab = 0 only when a = 0 or b = 0 (it is normed); by Hurwitz, R, C, H and O are the only normed division algebras", "inverses": "every a != 0 has a^-1 = conj(a)/|a|^2 (a a^-1 = 1, checked)", "conjugation": "conj(ab) = conj(b) conj(a) (checked); a conj(a) = |a|^2", "headline": "the quaternions: dimension 4 over the reals, basis 1, i, j, k"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "the quaternions: dimension 4 over the reals, basis 1, i, j, k\n  commutative: no: i j = k but j i = -k\n  associative: yes ((ab)c = a(bc) at 200 random triples); by Frobenius, R, C and H are the only associative real division algebras\n  alternative: yes ((aa)b = a(ab), (ba)a = b(aa) at 200 random pairs)\n  flexible and power-associative: yes ((ab)a = a(ba); powers a^n are well defined), as in every Cayley-Dickson algebra\n  normed (a composition algebra): yes, |ab| = |a||b| at 200 random pairs (Euler's four-square identity)\n  a division algebra: yes, ab = 0 only when a = 0 or b = 0 (it is normed); by Hurwitz, R, C, H and O are the only normed division algebras\n  inverses: every a != 0 has a^-1 = conj(a)/|a|^2 (a a^-1 = 1, checked)\n  conjugation: conj(ab) = conj(b) conj(a) (checked); a conj(a) = |a|^2\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 5, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "the octonions: dimension 8 over the reals, basis 1, e1, e2, e3, e4, e5, e6, e7\n  associative: no: (e1 e2) e4 = e7 but e1 (e2 e4) = -e7\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 5, "ok": true, "cmd": "algebra", "ucas": "algebra octonion associative", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "algebra", "associative": "no: (e1 e2) e4 = e7 but e1 (e2 e4) = -e7", "headline": "the octonions: dimension 8 over the reals, basis 1, e1, e2, e3, e4, e5, e6, e7"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "the octonions: dimension 8 over the reals, basis 1, e1, e2, e3, e4, e5, e6, e7\n  associative: no: (e1 e2) e4 = e7 but e1 (e2 e4) = -e7\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 6, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "the sedenions: dimension 16 over the reals, basis 1, e1, e2, e3, e4, e5, e6, e7, ...\n  a division algebra: no, it has zero divisors: (e1 - e10)(e4 + e15) = 0\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 6, "ok": true, "cmd": "algebra", "ucas": "algebra sedenion division", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "algebra", "a_division_algebra": "no, it has zero divisors: (e1 - e10)(e4 + e15) = 0", "headline": "the sedenions: dimension 16 over the reals, basis 1, e1, e2, e3, e4, e5, e6, e7, ..."}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "the sedenions: dimension 16 over the reals, basis 1, e1, e2, e3, e4, e5, e6, e7, ...\n  a division algebra: no, it has zero divisors: (e1 - e10)(e4 + e15) = 0\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 7, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "the cd(32) numbers: dimension 32 over the reals, basis 1, e1, e2, e3, e4, e5, e6, e7, ...\n  normed: no: |ab| != |a||b| (off by 0.732 at a random pair)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 7, "ok": true, "cmd": "algebra", "ucas": "algebra cd 32 normed", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "algebra", "normed": "no: |ab| != |a||b| (off by 0.732 at a random pair)", "headline": "the cd(32) numbers: dimension 32 over the reals, basis 1, e1, e2, e3, e4, e5, e6, e7, ..."}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "the cd(32) numbers: dimension 32 over the reals, basis 1, e1, e2, e3, e4, e5, e6, e7, ...\n  normed: no: |ab| != |a||b| (off by 0.732 at a random pair)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 8, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "the cd(32) numbers: dimension 32 over the reals, basis 1, e1, e2, e3, e4, e5, e6, e7, ...\n  flexible and power-associative: yes ((ab)a = a(ba); powers a^n are well defined), as in every Cayley-Dickson algebra\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 8, "ok": true, "cmd": "algebra", "ucas": "algebra cd 32 flexible", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "algebra", "flexible_and_power_associative": "yes ((ab)a = a(ba); powers a^n are well defined), as in every Cayley-Dickson algebra", "headline": "the cd(32) numbers: dimension 32 over the reals, basis 1, e1, e2, e3, e4, e5, e6, e7, ..."}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "the cd(32) numbers: dimension 32 over the reals, basis 1, e1, e2, e3, e4, e5, e6, e7, ...\n  flexible and power-associative: yes ((ab)a = a(ba); powers a^n are well defined), as in every Cayley-Dickson algebra\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 9, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "the quaternions have no zero divisors: |ab| = |a||b|, so ab = 0 only when a = 0 or b = 0\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 9, "ok": true, "cmd": "zerodivisors", "ucas": "zerodivisors quaternion", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "zerodivisors", "headline": "the quaternions have no zero divisors: |ab| = |a||b|, so ab = 0 only when a = 0 or b = 0"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "the quaternions have no zero divisors: |ab| = |a||b|, so ab = 0 only when a = 0 or b = 0\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 10, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "zero divisors in the sedenions:\n  (e1 - e10)(e4 + e15) = 0, although |e1 - e10| = |e4 + e15| = sqrt(2)\n  so |ab| = |a||b| fails and the sedenions are not a division algebra (from dimension 16 on, every Cayley-Dickson algebra has them)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 10, "ok": true, "cmd": "zerodivisors", "ucas": "zerodivisors sedenion", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "zerodivisors", "headline": "zero divisors in the sedenions:", "details": ["(e1 - e10)(e4 + e15) = 0, although |e1 - e10| = |e4 + e15| = sqrt(2)", "so |ab| = |a||b| fails and the sedenions are not a division algebra (from dimension 16 on, every Cayley-Dickson algebra has them)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "zero divisors in the sedenions:\n  (e1 - e10)(e4 + e15) = 0, although |e1 - e10| = |e4 + e15| = sqrt(2)\n  so |ab| = |a||b| fails and the sedenions are not a division algebra (from dimension 16 on, every Cayley-Dickson algebra has them)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 11, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "zero divisors in the cd(32) numbers:\n  (e1 - e10)(e4 + e15) = 0, although |e1 - e10| = |e4 + e15| = sqrt(2)\n  so |ab| = |a||b| fails and the cd(32) numbers are not a division algebra (from dimension 16 on, every Cayley-Dickson algebra has them)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 11, "ok": true, "cmd": "zerodivisors", "ucas": "zerodivisors cd 32", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "zerodivisors", "headline": "zero divisors in the cd(32) numbers:", "details": ["(e1 - e10)(e4 + e15) = 0, although |e1 - e10| = |e4 + e15| = sqrt(2)", "so |ab| = |a||b| fails and the cd(32) numbers are not a division algebra (from dimension 16 on, every Cayley-Dickson algebra has them)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "zero divisors in the cd(32) numbers:\n  (e1 - e10)(e4 + e15) = 0, although |e1 - e10| = |e4 + e15| = sqrt(2)\n  so |ab| = |a||b| fails and the cd(32) numbers are not a division algebra (from dimension 16 on, every Cayley-Dickson algebra has them)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 12, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = -1 - (-1) = 0\n  the product of these three is associative (in the quaternions)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 12, "ok": true, "cmd": "associator", "ucas": "associator i, j, k", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "associator", "headline": "[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = -1 - (-1) = 0", "details": ["the product of these three is associative (in the quaternions)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = -1 - (-1) = 0\n  the product of these three is associative (in the quaternions)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 13, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = e7 - (-e7) = 2 e7\n  not associative: the grouping changes the product (in the octonions)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 13, "ok": true, "cmd": "associator", "ucas": "associator e1, e2, e4", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "associator", "not_associative": "the grouping changes the product (in the octonions)", "headline": "[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = e7 - (-e7) = 2 e7"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = e7 - (-e7) = 2 e7\n  not associative: the grouping changes the product (in the octonions)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 14, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = -e19 - (e19) = -2 e19\n  not associative: the grouping changes the product (in the cd(32) numbers)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 14, "ok": true, "cmd": "associator", "ucas": "associator e16, e17, e18", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "associator", "not_associative": "the grouping changes the product (in the cd(32) numbers)", "headline": "[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = -e19 - (e19) = -2 e19"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "[a, b, c] = (ab)c - a(bc) = -e19 - (e19) = -2 e19\n  not associative: the grouping changes the product (in the cd(32) numbers)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 15, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "[a, b] = ab - ba = k - (-k) = 2k\n  they do not commute\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 15, "ok": true, "cmd": "commutator", "ucas": "commutator i, j", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "commutator", "headline": "[a, b] = ab - ba = k - (-k) = 2k", "details": ["they do not commute"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "[a, b] = ab - ba = k - (-k) = 2k\n  they do not commute\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 16, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "[a, b] = ab - ba = -e1 - (e1) = -2 e1\n  they do not commute\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 16, "ok": true, "cmd": "commutator", "ucas": "commutator e30, e31", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "commutator", "headline": "[a, b] = ab - ba = -e1 - (e1) = -2 e1", "details": ["they do not commute"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "[a, b] = ab - ba = -e1 - (e1) = -2 e1\n  they do not commute\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 17, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "rotate (1, 0, 0) by the quaternion 1 + i + j + k:\n  note: q is not a unit quaternion (|q| = 2): normalised\n  q = 1/2 + i/2 + j/2 + k/2: a rotation by 2pi/3 about (sqrt(3)/3, sqrt(3)/3, sqrt(3)/3)\n  v = i (the vector as a pure quaternion)\n  q v q^-1 = j\n  rotated: (0, 1, 0)\n  check: |v'| = |v| = 1, the real part is 0, and the rotation matrix gives the same vector\n  rotation matrix:\n    [0, 0, 1]\n    [1, 0, 0]\n    [0, 1, 0]\n  (right-handed: counterclockwise looking down the axis towards the origin; -q gives the same rotation)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 17, "ok": true, "cmd": "rotate", "ucas": "rotate (1, 0, 0) by 1+i+j+k", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "rotate", "q": "1/2 + i/2 + j/2 + k/2: a rotation by 2pi/3 about (sqrt(3)/3, sqrt(3)/3, sqrt(3)/3)", "v": "i (the vector as a pure quaternion)", "rotated": "(0, 1, 0)", "headline": "rotate (1, 0, 0) by the quaternion 1 + i + j + k:", "details": ["q v q^-1 = j", "rotation matrix:", "[0, 0, 1]", "[1, 0, 0]", "[0, 1, 0]", "(right-handed: counterclockwise looking down the axis towards the origin; -q gives the same rotation)"]}, "notes": [{"kind": "info", "text": "q is not a unit quaternion (|q| = 2): normalised"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "|v'| = |v| = 1, the real part is 0, and the rotation matrix gives the same vector"}], "files": [], "text": "rotate (1, 0, 0) by the quaternion 1 + i + j + k:\n  note: q is not a unit quaternion (|q| = 2): normalised\n  q = 1/2 + i/2 + j/2 + k/2: a rotation by 2pi/3 about (sqrt(3)/3, sqrt(3)/3, sqrt(3)/3)\n  v = i (the vector as a pure quaternion)\n  q v q^-1 = j\n  rotated: (0, 1, 0)\n  check: |v'| = |v| = 1, the real part is 0, and the rotation matrix gives the same vector\n  rotation matrix:\n    [0, 0, 1]\n    [1, 0, 0]\n    [0, 1, 0]\n  (right-handed: counterclockwise looking down the axis towards the origin; -q gives the same rotation)\n"}, "isError": false}}
